From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:09:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: stream: free the port array when the presence rate
 is rejected

slim_stream_prepare() allocates rt->ports before it looks up the
presence rate code, and the error path for an unsupported rate returns
without freeing it. rt->ports stays set, so the leak is not merely a
leak: the "Stream already Prepared" guard at the top of the function
then rejects every subsequent attempt to prepare the same stream, and a
caller that retries at a rate the bus does support is refused for the
lifetime of the runtime.

Free the array and clear the pointer, so the runtime is left in the
state it was in on entry.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/slimbus/stream.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/stream.c b/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
index 863ab3075d7e..738a23bb8131 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
@@ -227,6 +227,8 @@ int slim_stream_prepare(struct slim_stream_runtime *rt,
 	if (prrate < 0) {
 		dev_err(&rt->dev->dev, "Cannot get presence rate for rate %d Hz\n",
 			cfg->rate);
+		kfree(rt->ports);
+		rt->ports = NULL;
 		return prrate;
 	}
 
